<h2 id="200h-qigong-teacher-training">200-Hour Online Qigong Teacher Training</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom:1.2em;"><a href="/why-qigong-training/" style="font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Why choose this training?</a></p>

<div class="shared-story">
<p>A serious and in-depth professional training in authentic Qigong, designed for those who want to practise and teach with real understanding, precision and integrity.</p>
<p>This programme is for people seeking genuine internal development rather than surface-level wellness trends or movement imitation.</p>
</div>

<p>The training brings together traditional Qigong methods, internal principles and practical teaching skills in a structured and carefully guided format. Many of the practices included are rarely taught with this level of depth, clarity and direct correction.</p>

<p>Rather than simply learning sequences of movements, students are guided towards understanding how Qigong actually works internally:</p>

<ul class="features">
<li>Posture and alignment</li>
<li>Breath</li>
<li>Use of intention (Yi)</li>
<li>Energetic awareness</li>
<li>Meridian pathways</li>
<li>Acupuncture points</li>
<li>Internal mechanics</li>
<li>Gradual cultivation of skill through consistent practice</li>
</ul>

<p>The emphasis throughout the programme is precision, sensitivity and embodied understanding.</p>

<p>Students receive direct guidance and detailed correction throughout the training. This is not a passive "watch videos and get certified" course. Considerable attention is given to details that are often overlooked but make a profound difference to both practice and teaching ability.</p>

<p>The aim is not merely to complete a certification, but to establish a strong foundation for long-term practice, confident teaching and authentic internal development.</p>

<h3>What You Will Learn</h3>
<ul class="features">
<li>Five-Element Qigong forms taught progressively and in depth</li>
<li>Extraordinary-Meridian Qigong practices</li>
<li>Shen Qigong methods</li>
<li>Standing meditation (Zhan Zhuang)</li>
<li>Internal energy work and use of the Yi</li>
<li>Breathwork and energetic coordination</li>
<li>Meridian pathways and relevant acupuncture points</li>
<li>Foundations of Traditional Chinese Medicine relevant to Qigong</li>
<li>Teaching methodology and class structure</li>
<li>Practicum and mentored teaching practice</li>
</ul>

<h3>Who This Training Is For</h3>

<p>This training is suitable for:</p>

<ul class="features">
<li>Dedicated beginners</li>
<li>Experienced practitioners</li>
<li>Yoga teachers</li>
<li>Therapists</li>
<li>Bodyworkers</li>
<li>Movement educators</li>
<li>Those wishing to teach authentic Qigong with clarity and confidence</li>
</ul>

<p>No previous Qigong experience is required. What matters far more is sincerity, patience and willingness to practise consistently.</p>

<h3>Training Format</h3>
<ul class="features">
<li>200 hours total training</li>
<li>Approximately 100 hours of direct live teaching</li>
<li>Live online sessions</li>
<li>Additional recorded material for review and practice</li>
<li>Ongoing guidance and feedback throughout the programme</li>
<li>Internationally accessible</li>
</ul>

<h3>A Different Approach to Online Qigong Training</h3>

<p>Much of modern online Qigong focuses mainly on choreography, relaxation or vague concepts of "energy".</p>

<p>This training takes a different approach.</p>

<p>Strong emphasis is placed on the foundations that genuinely shape internal practice: alignment, awareness, intention, breath, energetic structure and gradual refinement through careful repetition and direct guidance.</p>

<p>The result is a training that supports not only learning forms, but developing real skill, sensitivity and confidence over time.</p>

<p>For pricing and availability, please <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>

